diag(pip): Log the stable overlay inputs while aiming, and note the motion blur

The thermal sight keeps its ring through the stable overlay fix, and the log explains why the fix
could not have helped: the pass lines in it belong to an ordinary optical sight (img=0), and the
sight the player is testing never appears in the optic lines, so the predicate's inputs for it were
never visible. What the log does show is that the camera motion blur is on (ssfx_motionblur 8, 0.1,
...), and that is a screen space effect driven by the scene motion vectors, applied to a sight whose
image is screen locked. On a flat, circular edged display that smear reads as a halo, it only exists
while the view moves, and my earlier gating of it covers the lens pass only - which a thermal optic
never runs, because the engine withholds its lens. That matches "the fix did nothing".

This adds both halves of the measurement. The stable overlay test now logs its inputs and result
once per 300 frames while the player is aiming (unstable, svp, magnifies, lensFov, ads, zoom,
motionblur, img), so the next test says whether the clause fires for a thermal optic; and the
motion blur can be ruled in or out immediately with "ssfx_motionblur 0, 0, 0, 0", which needs no
rebuild.